The French position on Usmanov is reportedly linked to an agreement to free two French citizens imprisoned in Azerbaijan, while Luxembourg pressured Fridman, who has initiated arbitration against the country seeking $16 billion in compensation for frozen assets. The decision was criticized by the Ukrainian government, which called it "shameful and unjustifiable"

